# Line endings are pinned to LF so generated artifacts are byte-identical across
# platforms. Without an explicit rule, core.autocrlf=true (common on Windows) checks
# text files out as CRLF; anything Chock then regenerates with LF is reported
# as modified by `git status` while `git diff` shows nothing -- noise that trains
# people to run `git checkout --` over generated output.
#
# Pair this with chock.emit.write_generated(), which writes LF regardless of
# platform. Both halves are required: the attribute governs checkout, the writer
# governs regeneration.

.git/hooks/** text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.txt text eol=lf
*.tmpl text eol=lf

# Generated trees: every file, including extensionless shims.
.chock/** text eol=lf

# Guard implementations are shell scripts named without extensions in some trees.
*/implementations/** text eol=lf
